    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "# **Holiday Sales: Statistical Significance**\n",
        "Holiday weeks show higher average sales than regular weeks in the dataset. To determine whether this difference is statistically significant, a paired-samples t-test is used to compare each store’s average holiday-week sales with the same store’s average regular-week sales.\n",
        "\n",
        "\n",
        "\n",
        "Average holiday-week sales are approximately \\$1.12 million per store, compared with approximately \\$1.04 million during regular weeks.\n"
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "id": "M8EwcjK8S-Jh"
      }
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "\n",
        "store_holiday = (\n",
        "    df.groupby([\"Store\", \"Holiday_Flag\"])[\"Weekly_Sales\"]\n",
        "      .mean()\n",
        "      .unstack()\n",
        ")\n",
        "\n",
        "t_stat, p_value = stats.ttest_rel(\n",
        "    store_holiday[1],\n",
        "    store_holiday[0]\n",
        ")\n",
        "\n",
        "print(\"T-statistic:\", t_stat)\n",
        "print(\"P-value:\", p_value)"
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "colab": {
          "base_uri": "https://localhost:8080/"
        },
        "id": "IJiyeWgmVOFg",
        "outputId": "be935f89-5487-4735-dcfa-9b736bdff69b"
      },
      "execution_count": 67,
      "outputs": [
        {
          "output_type": "stream",
          "name": "stdout",
          "text": [
            "T-statistic: 9.652455490862085\n",
            "P-value: 1.966293307021727e-12\n"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "Statistical Test Result\n",
        "\n",
        "The paired-samples t-test produced a t-statistic of approximately 9.65 and a p-value of approximately 1.97 × 10⁻¹², which is well below the 0.05 significance level.\n",
        "\n",
        "This provides strong statistical evidence that average sales differ between holiday and regular weeks across the stores in the dataset. However, statistical significance alone does not establish that holidays directly caused the increase in sales. Other seasonal or business-related factors may also contribute to the difference."
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "id": "4_IVgi0ukIIz"
      }
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "\n",
        "\n",
        "---\n",
        "\n"
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "id": "qToOoMKmeylh"
      }
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "# **Economic/Environmental Factors**\n",
        "\n",
        "\n",
        "**Temperature, Fuel Price, CPI, and Unemployment**\n",
        "\n",
        "This analysis examines whether temperature, fuel prices, CPI, and unemployment are associated with weekly sales. Pearson correlation coefficients are used to measure the strength and direction of the linear relationship between each factor and weekly sales.\n"
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "id": "KqxciEsjntpw"
      }
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "factors = [\"Weekly_Sales\", \"Temperature\", \"Fuel_Price\", \"CPI\", \"Unemployment\"]\n",
